(A book is a room you enter without knocking. The door is the) Tj T*
(margin, and the first line is the threshold. Everything after) Tj T*
(that is architecture: the width of the column, the weight of) Tj T*
(the paper, the small distance between what is said and what is) Tj T*
(meant.) Tj T*
/F2 11 Tf 0.18 0.18 0.20 rg 14.6 TL
0 -16.00 Td
(Waraq was built around that idea. Reading needs fewer) Tj T*
(instruments, not more. The page should sit close to the hand,) Tj T*
(the interface should disappear at the exact moment attention) Tj T*
(arrives, and nothing should blink for the sake of blinking.) Tj T*
/F2 11 Tf 0.18 0.18 0.20 rg 14.6 TL
0 -16.00 Td
(When we removed the toolbar from the top of the screen and let) Tj T*
(the words take the full frame, the pages started to feel) Tj T*
(longer in the good way, the way a quiet corridor feels longer) Tj T*
(than a busy street.) Tj T*
ET
